            <ArticleTitle>Acetabular dysplasia and failure of development of the ischiopubic synchondrosis: a report of three related cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>248-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three cases of acetabular dysplasia associated with failed ossification of the ischiopubic synchondrosis are presented. The patients are second-degree relatives and all skeletally mature with no evidence of other pathological process to delay ossification. A summary of the development of the inferior pubic ramus is presented and the literature of this unusual condition is reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
